<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan yarn rates ease on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan yarn rates ease on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates eased on Wednesday as local cotton prices fell, dealers said. Yarn prices were seen falling further this week.</p>
<p>Following are the rates in rupees supplied by the Pakistan</p>
<p>Yarn Merchants Association for 10-lb (4.54 kg) cone of 21</p>
<p>counts:			    Wednesday   March 8</p>
<p>    Suraiya Textile	    455	   470</p>
<p>    Taj Textile		  480	   490</p>
<p>    Globe			  475	   480</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
